+# Chromium AROS camera capture through VHI
+
+Status: hypothesis
+
+## Rationale
+
+The existing AROS factory always enumerates zero cameras. The validated
+uvc.library exposes real UVC cameras as VHI inputs after the synthetic input
+zero. Consume that ABI rather than USB directly. Each capture thread owns
+its library and handle; stop joins before releasing the client. The driver
+bounds capture waits. Fail on changed input names, invalid frames and capture
+errors rather than silently falling back to a test pattern.
+
+VHI RGB24 stores red first. Chromium previously only accepted RGB24 camera
+conversion on Linux/ChromeOS/Windows; AROS must select libyuv FOURCC_RAW.
+
+## Baseline and validation
+
+Draft based on observed Chromium 154e4ec5e2af5ada8866c0bdf903edd899a206fd.
+Claude coordination TRIG-1443/TRIG-1444 is pending before integration.
+Cross compilation of the backend, factory wiring and RGB24 conversion succeeds
+using recorded existing CEF build commands with private output files. Existing
+base/containers/span.h constexpr warnings persist. This is not browser runtime
+proof. Live getUserMedia, stop/reopen and device-removal tests remain required.
+
+Evidence: /run/media/terminills/Codex/adt-uvc-01a15bd6/evidence/chromium-capture-draft
+Relay: JOB-0212 (parent JOB-0066)
